# name: The stranger
The stranger in the grey coat has not moved since the jetty. Now they turn to you.
"You know this river better than anyone alive. What will you do tomorrow, when it has a bridge?" # speaker: stranger
* ["I'll find other work."]
  "Will you." It isn't a question. # speaker: stranger
* ["I'll still be here, on the water."]
  # fx: set-flag(flag: stranger-named, to: true)
  The stranger laughs, a sound like the weir.
  "Then I'll tell you my name. Some nights it's a river's, and some nights it's yours." # speaker: stranger
- They look away, at the far bank coming up out of the dark.
-> END
